.TH CTI-APPREPORT 1 "2026-10-24" "cti-agent 1.4" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-appreport \- fetch the scanner's own report for each web application, zipped, to attach to its AppSec Jira ticket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti-appreport \-\-check
.PP
.B cti-appreport
.BI \-\-app\-id " ID"
.RB [ \-\-dump\-request ]
.RB [ \-\-request\-file
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-app\-name
.IR NAME ]
.PP
.B cti-appreport
.BI \-\-app\-id " ID"
.BI \-\-out\-dir " DIR"
.RB [ \-\-app\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-keep ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.RB [ \-\-request\-file
.IR FILE ]
.PP
.B cti-appreport
.BI \-\-tickets " FILE"
.BI \-\-out\-dir " DIR"
.RB [ \-\-only\-ref
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-reports
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-keep ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.PP
.B cti-appreport
.BI \-\-probe\-findings " ID"
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-appreport
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-appreport
asks the DAST scanner for its own report on a web application (the request
and response behind each finding, laid out the way the scanner documents
them) and writes it as a zip file for
.BR "cti\-jira \-\-appscan\-reports" .
For Qualys WAS the report is created, polled until it is ready, downloaded
as HTML_ZIPPED, and deleted from Qualys again. Only vulnerabilities in the
open states (NEW, ACTIVE, REOPENED) are reported.
.PP
It is normally run by
.BR run\-appscan (1)
when
.B WAS_ATTACH_REPORT=1
and by hand while testing. It writes files and never writes to Jira: a
report reaches a ticket only if
.I reports.json
in the output directory lists it.
.PP
The scanner is chosen by
.BR APPSCAN_REPORT_PROVIDER .
The commands reach it only through the Go interface
.IR appscan.ReportFetcher ,
so supporting another scanner is a package implementing that interface and
one case in the command's provider switch; nothing in
.BR cti\-jira (1)
or the runner changes.
.PP
.B Each report carries the scan account's session cookies
(the scanner records the requests it sent). Treat the directory like a
credential: files are written 0600 in a directory created 0700, the report
is deleted from the scanner after download (unless
.BR \-\-keep ),
and
.B run\-appscan
deletes the directory once the tickets are done.
.PP
.B It spends the shared Qualys API budget.
A report is about five calls. Every response's rate-limit and concurrency
headers are read (see
.BR QUALYS_RL_RESERVE ):
a short refusal is waited out, and the optional report work gives way when
only the reserve is left, so the vulnerability lane and KnowledgeBase
lookups are not starved. In the weekly run only applications whose ticket
will be filed or commented are fetched.
.PP
A report that cannot be fetched is not fatal: the ticket still carries
every finding and says nothing about an attachment that is not there.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash
.RB ( \-check ),
and a value may follow
.B =
or a space.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-ids
Print the web application id, name, confirmed and potential finding counts,
and whether a report would be fetched, for every application in the newest
.I $FLEET_HOME/state/appscan\-tickets\-<date>.json
(the weekly run's tickets file), or in the
.B \-\-tickets
file when one is given; then exit. Reads the file only: no scanner calls,
no credentials. The ids to try
.B \-\-app\-id
with.
Default:\~off.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Make one cheap authenticated call, print whether the credentials work, how
many web applications are defined, and the scanner's rate-limit position,
then exit. Writes nothing.
Default:\~off.
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-id " ID"
Fetch the report for this one web application id (a test). Needs
.B \-\-out\-dir
unless
.B \-\-dump\-request
is given.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-name " NAME"
With
.BR \-\-app\-id :
the name used in messages and the report title.
Default:\~\fBweb app\fR \fIID\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-tickets " FILE"
Fetch a report for every application in this
.B cti\-appscan \-\-tickets\-out
file that has findings and was not skipped. Needs
.BR \-\-out\-dir .
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-only\-ref " FILE"
With
.BR \-\-tickets :
a
.B cti\-jira \-\-ref\-out
preview file; fetch only the applications whose ticket would be filed or
commented (would-create, would-comment), never the unchanged ones.
Default:\~empty (every eligible application).
.TP
.BI \-\-out\-dir " DIR"
Write each report as
.IR LABEL .zip
and
.I reports.json
here, mode 0600; the directory is created 0700 if missing.
.I reports.json
lists what was fetched and, separately, what failed and why.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-reports " N"
Fetch at most this many reports in one run; the rest are listed as not
fetched.
Default:\~\fB30\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Leave each report in the scanner instead of deleting it (debugging). Reports
left behind count against the scanner's report limit; delete them in the
Qualys console.
Default:\~off.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Give up on one report after this long, create to download, as a Go
duration.
Default:\~\fB10m0s\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-request
With
.BR \-\-app\-id :
print the request that creates the report and send nothing.
Default:\~off.
.TP
.BI \-\-request\-file " FILE"
Send this create-report body instead of the built-in one.
.B {{APP_ID}}
and
.B {{NAME}}
are filled in. For correcting a field name while probing the live API,
without a rebuild.
Default:\~empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-probe\-findings " ID"
Print the scanner's verbose finding search for this web application id
(three open vulnerabilities) and exit. Cookie, Set-Cookie and Authorization
values are redacted from the output, which is still evidence from the
organisation's own application: redirect it to a 0600 file and keep it off
tickets.
Default:\~empty.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.I fleet.env
is loaded at start from
.B FLEET_ENV
(else
.IR $FLEET_HOME/fleet.env ,
else
.IR /var/lib/cti\-agent/fleet.env );
variables already in the environment win. Only the scanner's settings are
needed: no mailbox and no Jira.
.TP
.BR QUALYS_BASE_URL ", " QUALYS_USERNAME ", " QUALYS_PASSWORD
The WAS API. Required for the
.B qualys\-was
provider. Section 2.
.TP
.B APPSCAN_REPORT_PROVIDER
Which scanner's report to fetch. Default:\~\fBqualys\-was\fR (also
.BR qualys ).
An unknown name is an error that lists the known ones.
.TP
.B QUALYS_RL_RESERVE
Calls to leave unspent in the current rate-limit window for the vulnerability
lane and KnowledgeBase lookups. When only this many remain, report work
stops and the rest is listed as not fetched.
Default:\~\fB5\fR.
.TP
.B QUALYS_RL_MAX_WAIT
The longest the client will sleep for a rate-limit or concurrency refusal,
as a Go duration. A longer wait is reported as an error instead.
Default:\~\fB5m\fR.
.PP
The limiter follows the limits Qualys reports in its response headers, so
there is nothing to change when the subscription's limits are raised.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR DIR /reports.json
The manifest:
provider, generation time, each fetched report (file, size, scanner report
id) and each failure. 0600.
.TP
.IR DIR / LABEL .zip
One application's report, 0600. The label is the ticket label
.RB ( cti\-appscan\- \fIid\fR ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command did what was asked. With
.BR \-\-tickets ,
reports that could not be fetched are a warning, not a failure.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration missing or invalid, an unknown provider, a rejected option
combination, the scanner refused, or (with
.BR \-\-app\-id )
the report was not fetched.
.TP
.B 2
An unknown option or an unparseable duration.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the credentials and the rate-limit position:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-appreport \-\-check
.EE
.PP
Show the request without sending it:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-appreport \-\-app\-id 123456 \-\-dump\-request
.EE
.PP
Fetch one report, leave it in Qualys to look at, then do it again cleanly:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent cti\-appreport \-\-app\-id 123456 \-\-out\-dir /tmp/r \-\-keep
sudo cti\-agent cti\-appreport \-\-app\-id 123456 \-\-out\-dir /tmp/r
.EE
.PP
Look at the raw finding fields (redacted) in a private file:
.PP
.EX
(umask 077; sudo cti\-agent cti\-appreport \-\-probe\-findings 123456 > /tmp/probe.xml)
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-appscan (1),
.BR cti\-jira (1),
.BR cti\-appscan (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 11f; fleet\-kit/README.md, "The weekly AppSec report".
